    "body": "## Summary\n- persist Stripe payment dispute exposure and signed event idempotency with Flyway V47\n- process `charge.dispute.created`, `updated`, `closed`, `funds_withdrawn`, and `funds_reinstated`\n- use Stripe balance-movement events, not dispute status strings, as financial authority\n- recover only free wallet balance without ever making the immutable wallet ledger negative\n- block ordinary outgoing wallet debits while chargeback exposure remains outstanding\n- retry recovery of later incoming wallet credits with an idempotent scheduled worker\n- reinstate only funds that doFast actually recovered from the user's wallet\n- handle out-of-order withdrawal/reinstatement delivery safely\n- add focused unit tests, operator documentation, and a signed-webhook PostgreSQL runtime smoke\n\n## Risk boundary\nThis contains requester-side chargeback exposure but does not yet implement source-of-funds/provenance buckets. If disputed funding has already left escrow and been paid to a worker, the platform can temporarily carry that exposure while the requester wallet is restricted and recovered over time. Provider dispute evidence/representment is also out of scope.\n\n## Validation required before merge\n- exact latest-head Maven/API verify\n- frontend test/audit/lint/build\n- Production Compose contract\n- full containers/runtime smoke\n- Payments ledger smoke including the signed Stripe chargeback scenario\n- any other path-triggered financial workflows\n\nMerge only when every required latest-head workflow is green. Use a merge commit, not squash.",
